  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full set at the Vega in Lincoln, Nebraska, on September 10, 2015 [1]. This recording captures twenty-one songs over approximately eighty minutes, representing show 212 in the archive’s collection for the band [2]. The setlist opens with “Surrounded” and “Linda Blair Was Born Innocent” before moving into “There Will Be No Divorce” and “Werewolf Gimmick” [1]. Later in the main set, the band plays “The Day the Aliens Came (Hawaiian Feeling),” a track that had not appeared in 35 archived shows prior to this date [2]. Other main set selections include “Dance Music,” “Heel Turn 2,” and “Southwestern Territory” [1]. The performance features spoken introductions for the song “Thank You Mario But Our Princess is in Another Castle” [1]. The set concludes with “Up the Wolves” before the band returns for an encore [1]. The encore includes “I Hope You Dance,” identified in the uploader’s description as a Lee Ann Womack cover, which is the first appearance of this song in the archive [1][2]. The final two songs are “No Children” and “The Best Ever Death Metal Band in Denton” [1]. This is the only available recording of this specific show, making it the recommended source for listeners interested in this performance [1]. The previous archived show for the band occurred at the Mayan Theater on June 3, 2015 [2].",
